<title>MEXICO: GEC Alsthom signs 271.13 mln peso Mexico metro fix.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom signs 271.13 mln peso Mexico metro fix.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's GEC Alsthom agreed Monday to repair 234 cars of Mexico City's metro in the next two years for 271.13 million pesos, government news agency Notimex reported.</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom is a joint venture of Alcatal Alsthom and GEC Plc.</p>
<p>The cars have been in use for more than 20 years, and with the repairs should last another 20, GEC Alsthom and city officials told reporters.</p>
<p>Financing for the Mexico City project will come from credits from government development banks in both countries.</p>
<p>((--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-7903))</p>
